{"commands":[{"command":"anchor headers sync","summary":"validate Bitcoin block headers from a file and persist them as this reader's chain view"},{"command":"anchor stamp","summary":"timestamp a line of your log: submit its id to OpenTimestamps calendars and commit the pending proof with an anchors statement"},{"command":"anchor status","summary":"this reader's chain backend: provider, mode, network, bootstrap, tip, last sync, freshness, receipt count"},{"command":"anchor upgrade","summary":"complete pending timestamps: ask the calendars for the Bitcoin path of each pending proof and commit an upgraded anchors statement"},{"command":"explain","summary":"the statements, policy, evaluator and time context behind every token shown"},{"command":"fetch","summary":"obtain blobs from the locations held `holds` statements name, verified by full hash; never publishes a holds"},{"command":"fsck","summary":"check the store: blobs re-hashed, statements re-read, references resolved, journal and cache checked"},{"command":"gc","summary":"list (default) or delete unreferenced blobs outside the grace window; release a blob this store serves"},{"command":"history","summary":"list operations this store finished, newest first (local, not authoritative)"},{"command":"hub check","summary":"check a change to the hub this directory is in, as the hub's CI does (writes nothing)"},{"command":"identity cut","summary":"cut a grant: the delegate's acts after --last-good stop counting for the identity"},{"command":"identity grant","summary":"grant a delegate key the right to act for an identity"},{"command":"identity new","summary":"create a fixed-root identity: sign its inception with a fresh root key"},{"command":"init","summary":"create a store in a directory (default: the working directory)"},{"command":"key new","summary":"generate a signing key into a new file (mode 0600, never overwritten)"},{"command":"key show","summary":"print the signer and algorithm of a key file (never the key), or of a Ledger device's key"},{"command":"key sign","summary":"sign an external-signing package's PAE bytes with a key file (reads no store)"},{"command":"list","summary":"every blob a statement in this store names, and every resource, one line of tokens each"},{"command":"package show","summary":"check an external-signing package and print what its signature would cover (reads no store)"},{"command":"publish","summary":"sign and commit a statement (authored with its bytes, holds, describes, retracts, or a draft)"},{"command":"publish grant","summary":"sign a task coordinator's grant for one edition"},{"command":"publish task","summary":"create a task (genesis + first edition) or publish a new edition of one"},{"command":"pull","summary":"admit a package (a store tree in a directory or a tar archive) into this store under this reader's policy"},{"command":"push","summary":"judge the commits of this hub checkout as the hub's CI would, apply the anchor and withheld-bytes preconditions, and when all is clean git push the judged commit (never forced; --dry-run sends nothing)"},{"command":"repair","summary":"finish committed operations the store could not finish: reinstall, re-check blobs, rebuild projections"},{"command":"revoke","summary":"revoke your signing key: sign a revoke_key whose history keeps what you choose"},{"command":"rotate","summary":"rotate your signing key: sign a rotate_key naming its successor"},{"command":"run","summary":"run a held workflow under your execution policy; --publish signs what it emits"},{"command":"show","summary":"show a blob (authorship, grade, every disclosure), a statement, a resource, or a key"},{"command":"status","summary":"store recovery state, unfinished operations and the durability declaration"},{"command":"verify","summary":"check a blob or a statement from the statements held; exit per the exit table"}],"global_options":[{"option":"--json","summary":"print one JSON object on stdout (an RFC 9457 problem-details object on error)"},{"option":"--store","summary":"the store to read (default: $COMMONS_STORE, else the nearest ancestor directory holding rc-store)"},{"option":"--help","summary":"print help for the command and exit 0"},{"option":"--version","summary":"print the version and exit 0"}],"more":"commons help <command> · commons help outputs (state tokens) · commons help exits (exit codes)","usage":"commons <command> [options] [--json]"}
